1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.comune.alzano.bg.it/vivere-il-comune/luoghi/architettura-residenziale/villa-augusto-pesenti-villa-camilla
2 CONT
2 CONT https://grokipedia.com/page/pesenti_family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://loreph.it/portfolio-item/105-villa-camilla/ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citat: 
2 CONT Villa Camilla was built to a design by architect Virginio Muzio as a wedding gift that Augusto Pesenti, an important cement entrepreneur, gave to his new bride Camilla Donadoni.  The same entrepreneur played a fundamental role in 
2 CONC the construction of the villa: taking advantage of the many business trips abroad, Pesenti sent illustrated postcards explaining to the architect how he would have liked some details of the villa.
2 CONT The villa was built in 1895 in typical neo-Renaissance style. Besides being a prestigious residence that represented the prestige of the family, it was designed to offer the family all the most innovative and modern comforts: in f
2 CONC act, it was equipped with toilets, running water, heating and radiators. All extremely modern innovations for a building of the time. Another peculiarity of this villa was the use of cement, the main product of the family business
2 CONC . Cement was used externally to create a cladding that simulated stone, to create columns, capitals and bas-reliefs; the flooring of many areas of the villa was also made of white cement tiles with the addition of different pigmen
2 CONC ts. Finally also the van stairs were made of cement granite, with a frame (also in cement) that looks like marble.
2 CONT The villa is surrounded by a large garden of 20,000 square metres in which there is also a beautiful oriental style greenhouse and stables. After years of degradation and carelessness, the villa has recently been secured and put u
2 CONC p for sale by the current owners. Next to the villa there is the historical Pesenti cement factory.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://loreph.it/portfolio-item/018-italcementi-alzano-lombardo/
