1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_Facchinetti
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Francesco Facchinetti''' (born May 2, 1980), also known as '''Dj Francesco''' or as '''Oz''', is an Italian DJ, producer, singer, musician and TV presenter.
2 CONT He rose to fame as a singer during the summer of 2003, when he released his debut single, ''"La canzone del capitano"'', which became a hit in Italy. Before retiring from his music career in 2007, he released three studio albums, 
2 CONC and he competed in the Sanremo Music Festival three times. He is the founder of Italian EDM trio "We Are PresidentS".
2 CONT In 2004, he was also a contestant of the Italian reality show L'isola dei famosi. Three years later, he became the co-presented of the show. Starting from 2008, Facchinetti presented the first four series of X Factor, the Italian 
2 CONC version of the talent show created by Simon Cowell in the United Kingdom. When RAI decided to discontinue the show, Facchinetti presented Star Academy, which replaced X Factor. Together with his father [https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Roby-Facchinetti/6000000068435126823 Roby Facchinetti], he was part of a duo coach on the third series of talent show The Voice of Italy. He was one of the Italian commentators for the second and third seasons of Netflix's Ultima
2 CONC te Beastmaster alongside Bianca Balti. 
