2 CONT '''GEDCOM Notes'''
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Baron of Casalnuovo''' 
2 CONT 9. — Giacomo Maria Saccano and Lanza; he took investiture of the fiefdom of Casalnuovo on 20 September 1570, as the eldest son and undoubted successor of Antonella, his mother (Conservatoria, cited place, year 1570-96, sheet 8 on 
2 CONC the back). His first marriage was D. Topazia Valdina; he married in his second marriage D.na Beatrice Tagliavia-Aragona and Branciforte, daughter of Cav. of S. Giacomo Giuseppe and Francesca Branciforte (Mazarin). Which D. Giusepp
2 CONC e was the younger brother of the 1st Duke of Newfoundland D. Carlo Tagliavia-Aragona. Beatrice was already the widow of D. Gaspare Naselli 1st Count of Comiso and B.ne della Mastra and Diesi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage chapters between her and B.ne Saccano were stipulated by not. Giulio Pompeano from Messina on 8 July 1588. Blessed Beatrice died in Palermo between 10 and 13 January 1596. Her will was opened and published there in th
2 CONC e records of Notar Giovanni Aloisio Gandolfo on the 14th of that month and year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Barone Saccano died in Messina; his will was published by Not. Vespasiano Parisi of that city dated 4 February 1598 (see VILLAB., Sic. Nob., Vol. IV, page 190, note 6; and volume III, page 209, note a).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Prince of Monforte'''
2 CONT 12. — Giacomo Maria Saccano Laura took over the B.nia and Land of Monforte and Samperi, on 4 December 1570, as the eldest son and on the death of Baldassare, her father (R. Cancell., IV, Indiz., Foglio 117 and 118). His first marr
2 CONC iage was Diana Branciforte di Giovanni, Count of Mazzarino and Emilia Moncada. He married Beatrice Aragona Branciforte, widow of Gaspare Naselli, Count of Comiso (Dotali in Not.Giulio Pompeano, 8 April 1588 (VILLAB., Sic. Nob., vo
2 CONC lume 4°, page 190). He died in 1598; his will is in the records of Not. Parisi of Messina dated 3 February of that year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord of the Tonnara of the Port of Milazzo'''
2 CONT 6. — Giacomo Maria Saccano took over the Tonnara on 3 December 1570 following the death of Baldassare, his father (II. Cancelleria. XIV Indizione, folio 116). His first marriage was Topazia Valdina, daughter of Francesco Barone di
2 CONC  Rocca: his second marriage was Beatrice Aragona Branciforte, widow of Gaspare Naselli, Count of Comiso. The dowries of this second marriage, in Notary Giulio Pompeano dated 8 July 1588. His will is in Notar Vespasiano Barisi of M
2 CONC essina, on 3 February 1598.
